lessons.learnMarkdown:
## Phones, tablets and laptops

People visit websites on all kinds of screens. A page that looks great on a laptop can be squished on a phone. **Responsive design** means your page changes shape to fit the screen.

### Media queries

A **media query** is a CSS rule that only works on some screens:

```css
@media (max-width: 600px) {
  .cards {
    flex-direction: column;
  }
}
```

That says: *"When the screen is 600px wide or less, stack the cards in a column instead of a row."*

On big screens, the cards sit side by side. On small screens, they stack, so nothing gets squished.

### Stretchy pictures

`max-width: 100%;` on images stops them from poking out of small screens.

### New words

- **Responsive design**: pages that fit any screen size.
- **Media query**: CSS that only applies when a condition is true, like a small screen.

